 "issue": 1812,
 "issue_title": "Bug: validate write_parquet compression type before codec lookup",
 "issue_body": "## Summary\n\n`write_parquet()` does not validate the `compression` argument type before checking membership in the supported codec set.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nThe public docs describe `compression` as a string option. Passing an invalid non-string value should produce a clear Arnio-facing validation error, not a raw Python error such as `TypeError: unhashable type: 'list'`.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `arnio/io.py`: `write_parquet()` checks `if compression not in _VALID_COMPRESSIONS` without first validating that `compression` is a string.\n- `tests/test_parquet.py` covers unknown string compression values and `row_group_size` type validation, but does not cover non-string compression inputs.\n\n## Reproduction or trigger\n\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\nimport arnio as ar\n\nframe = ar.from_pandas(pd.DataFrame({\"a\": [1]}))\nar.write_parquet(frame, \"out.parquet\", compression=[\"snappy\"])\n```\n\n## Expected behavior\n\nA clear `TypeError`, for example `compression must be a string`, before codec validation.\n\n## Actual behavior\n\nA raw Python error is raised:\n\n```text\nTypeError: unhashable type: 'list'\n```\n\nOther non-string values such as `None`, `123`, or `True` currently produce `ValueError: Unknown compression codec`, which is also less precise than a type error.\n\n## Suggested direction\n\nAdd explicit type validation for `compression` before the membership check, and add tests for non-string values such as `None`, `123`, `True`, and `['snappy']`.\n\n## References\n\n- `arnio/io.py`\n- `tests/test_parquet.py`\r\n",
 "issue_url": "https://github.com/im-anishraj/arnio/issues/1812",
 "pr": 1866,
 "pr_title": "fix(io): validate parquet compression argument type",
 "pr_body": "### Fixes #1812 \r\n\r\n## Summary\r\n\r\nAdds explicit type validation for the `compression` argument in `write_parquet()` before codec membership validation.\r\n\r\n## Problem\r\n\r\n`write_parquet()` previously checked:\r\n\r\n```python\r\nif compression not in _VALID_COMPRESSIONS:\r\n```\r\n\r\nwithout first validating that `compression` was a string.\r\n\r\nThis caused invalid non-string values such as:\r\n\r\n```python\r\nNone\r\n123\r\nTrue\r\n[\"snappy\"]\r\n```\r\n\r\nto raise inconsistent or raw Python errors like:\r\n\r\n```txt\r\nTypeError: unhashable type: 'list'\r\n```\r\n\r\ninstead of a clear Arnio-facing validation error.\r\n\r\n## Changes made\r\n\r\n- Added explicit type validation for the `compression` argument\r\n- Non-string compression values now raise:\r\n  ```python\r\n  TypeError(\"compression must be a string\")\r\n  ```\r\n- Preserved existing behavior for unsupported string codecs:\r\n  ```python\r\n  compression=\"lz4\"\r\n  ```\r\n  still raises:\r\n  ```python\r\n  ValueError(\"Unknown compression codec\")\r\n  ```\r\n- Added parametrized regression tests covering:\r\n  - `None`\r\n  - `123`\r\n  - `True`\r\n  - `[\"snappy\"]`\r\n\r\n## Result\r\n\r\n`write_parquet()` now produces clearer and more consistent validation errors for invalid compression argument types while preserving existing codec validation behavior.\r\n",
